Bound dashed stroke expansion per SVG render.

Telegram-originated hardening, not an upstream backport. It requires
qtbase_6.11.2/0075-bound-dash-expansion-per-render.patch, whose private
QDashBudget lets QtGui charge the dash loop iterations of QDashStroker
and of the raster engine's dashed lines, and the outline geometry their
dashes add, to one pair of allowances. QtGui alone limits dash
repetitions only per segment or per line, so an untrusted SVG repeating
such segments over many paths, references and nested offscreen images
could emit hundreds of millions of dashes from a few kilobytes.

Each draw of an untrusted document, and each uncached bounds pass, which
can render pattern images, now arms one QDashBudget of
QtSvg::renderingMaxDashSteps (65536) iterations and
QtSvg::renderingMaxDashGeometry (2^20) geometry units, through
QSvgRenderBudget::DrawScope, defined in the new private header
qsvgdrawscope_p.h so that only its three users include qstroker_p.h.
All painting on that thread until it returns, on the target painter and
in the filter, mask, pattern and group opacity images drawn meanwhile,
spends those allowances, and a draw or bounds pass nested in it adds
none. A dashed segment or line that no longer fits is drawn solid, as at
Qt's repetition limit; the qtbase patch describes the units and the
rarer skips. AssumeTrustedSource documents, which have no render budget,
arm nothing.

